Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-rs6000.c
Line: 3934
Function: xcoff_ppc_relocate_section
Bug type: out-of-bounds-write
CWE: CWE-787
Explanation: After the same insufficient bounds check (only address > input_section->size), the code writes 2 or 4 bytes back to contents+address via bfd_put_16/bfd_put_32 without verifying address + reloc_size <= input_section->size. If address is at or near the end of the section, this causes an out-of-bounds write.

